avviato file_bridge. control_panell ok; pannelli vifm danno "warning checkinf for string using a boolean context is a bug; per usermail ho userlan color scheme is not supported. Ecco gli schemi che uso per xterm: 1) userdoc: -bg darkgreen -fg white; 2) usermail: -bg darkorchid3 -fg white ; 3) userweb: -bg darkblue -fg white;      Due problemi: il warning di vifm e i colori xterm. Sistemiamoli.
1. Warning vifm
È un bug noto di vifm quando riceve comandi via -c. Si risolve racchiudendo ogni cmap in un blocco che forza il contesto corretto:
-c 'cmap <f5> qcp'   →   -c 'execute "cmap <f5> qcp"'

2. Colori xterm
run_app non propaga le variabili d'ambiente del terminale del conductor ai domini. Devi passare i colori esplicitamente. xterm accetta -bg e -fg da riga di comando.
Ecco lo script corretto:
#!/bin/ksh
# ==========================================================
#  dropQbsd -- file_bridge
#
#  tmux-based 4-quadrant file manager bridge across all
#  three dropQbsd domains. Each domain gets its own vifm
#  :only instance launched via run_app, with qcp/qmv/qimport
#  bound to F5/F6/F7. control_panel sits in the top-left
#  quadrant for real-time drop zone and compartment status.
#
#  No config files in domain homes. No hardcoded geometry.
#  vifm keybindings are injected via command-line flags.
#  tiled layout adapts to terminal size automatically.
#
#  Path: /opt/dropQbsd/bin/file_bridge
#  Permissions: chmod 755, root:wheel
#  Usage: file_bridge
#
#  Requirements: tmux, vifm, control_panel
# ==========================================================

SESSION="file_bridge"

# -- Teardown existing session -----------------------------

tmux kill-session -t "$SESSION" 2>/dev/null
sleep 0.3

# -- Quadrant 1: top-left, control_panel -------------------

tmux new-session -d -s "$SESSION" -n 'bridge' \
    "control_panel"

# -- Quadrant 2: top-right, userdoc ------------------------

tmux split-window -h -t "$SESSION:0" \
    "xterm -bg darkgreen -fg white \
     -e /opt/dropQbsd/bin/run_app userdoc vifm +only \
     -c 'execute \"cmap <f5> qcp\"' \
     -c 'execute \"cmap <f6> qmv\"' \
     -c 'execute \"cmap <f7> qimport\"' \
     /home/userdoc"

# -- Quadrant 3: bottom-left, usermail ---------------------

tmux select-pane -t "$SESSION:0.0"
tmux split-window -v -t "$SESSION:0.0" \
    "xterm -bg darkorchid3 -fg white \
     -e /opt/dropQbsd/bin/run_app usermail vifm +only \
     -c 'execute \"cmap <f5> qcp\"' \
     -c 'execute \"cmap <f6> qmv\"' \
     -c 'execute \"cmap <f7> qimport\"' \
     /home/usermail"

# -- Quadrant 4: bottom-right, userweb ─────────────────────

tmux select-pane -t "$SESSION:0.1"
tmux split-window -v -t "$SESSION:0.1" \
    "xterm -bg darkblue -fg white \
     -e /opt/dropQbsd/bin/run_app userweb vifm +only \
     -c 'execute \"cmap <f5> qcp\"' \
     -c 'execute \"cmap <f6> qmv\"' \
     -c 'execute \"cmap <f7> qimport\"' \
     /home/userweb"

# -- Even layout -------------------------------------------

tmux select-layout -t "$SESSION" tiled

# -- Style -------------------------------------------------

tmux set-option -t "$SESSION" pane-border-style 'fg=#444444'
tmux set-option -t "$SESSION" pane-active-border-style 'fg=#FFFFFF'

tmux select-pane -t "$SESSION:0.0" -T "control"
tmux select-pane -t "$SESSION:0.1" -T "userdoc"
tmux select-pane -t "$SESSION:0.2" -T "usermail"
tmux select-pane -t "$SESSION:0.3" -T "userweb"

# -- Attach -----------------------------------------------
